# TypeScript Patterns and Conventions for SPOTS

## Configuration
- TypeScript config in [tsconfig.json](mdc:spots-app/tsconfig.json)
- Path aliases configured: `@/*` maps to root directory
- Strict mode enabled for type safety
- Next.js types included automatically

## Type Definitions (Developer 3 Focus)
- Define interfaces for all business logic data structures
- Use proper typing for business logic models with `*-business.ts` naming
- Reference schema types from [amplify/data/resource.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/data/resource.ts)
- Export business logic types for reuse across services and hooks
- Create strict TypeScript interfaces for PRO-CTCAE compliance

## Component Patterns (Developer 3 Focus)
- Use TypeScript interfaces for business logic component props
- Define proper return types for business logic functions
- Use React.FC or explicit return types for business logic components
- Implement proper error handling with typed errors for business logic
- Focus on business logic components rather than UI components

## AWS Amplify Integration
- Import types from generated schema
- Use typed Data client: `generateClient<Schema>()`
- Define proper interfaces for auth user data
- Type all API responses and requests

## Data Models
Reference the User model from [amplify/data/resource.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/data/resource.ts):
```typescript
interface User {
  email: string;
  role: string;
  givenName?: string;
  familyName?: string;
  createdAt?: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
}
```

## Error Handling
- Define custom error types
- Use proper error boundaries with TypeScript
- Implement typed error responses
- Handle async operations with proper typing

## State Management (Developer 3 Focus)
- Use TypeScript for all business logic state definitions
- Define proper types for business logic data structures
- Implement typed event handlers for business logic
- Use proper typing for custom React hooks with business logic
- Focus on complex state management for symptoms, cart, and search

## API Integration (Developer 3 Focus)
- Type all business logic API endpoints and responses
- Define interfaces for Developer 1's backend API data
- Use proper typing for REST API operations
- Implement typed data fetching patterns for business logic
- Focus on integration with Developer 1's REDCap APIs
